  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted (config_027) is the clear best at 0.725 acc, and all four aggregation/fusion combos for that pair have been tested. The only untested RNA encoder in this top architecture is pca_n2000. This experiment tests whether a linear PCA-based RNA representation can match the learned scvi_n200 VAE encoder under the best-performing multimodal setup (imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, multiprofile). If pca_n2000 is significantly worse (expected), it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and the current best is near-optimal, allowing the final experiment to target a minor refinement. If it is surprisingly competitive, it opens a cheaper alternative for the last slot. Cost: pca_n2000 is a simple linear projection (no VAE training), so expected training cost is modest—roughly 3–4 GPU hours, comparable to or slightly below config_027's 3.60 h, making it a low-cost, high-information experiment given only one run remains after this one."
}

